# SEO — public route registry (always-on)

**Non-negotiable:** a new or changed **public guest route** is classified in
`ui/src/lib/seo/publicRoutes.ts` in the same change. `bun run check:seo-routes` fails CI
otherwise, and it is part of `ci:quality`.

Full reference: **`docs/architecture/seo.md`**. Skill: **`seo`**.

## Every public route needs a registry entry

| Field         | Decide                                                             |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `indexable`   | Should a stranger land here from a search result or an AI answer?  |
| `inSitemap`   | Static pages only. Dynamic URLs come from `public_listing_search`. |
| `canonical`   | `self`, `listing` (needs edge data), or `none`.                    |
| `snapshot`    | `static`, `listing`, `place`, `host`, or `none`.                   |
| `title`       | Required for `snapshot: 'static'`.                                 |
| `description` | Required for `snapshot: 'static'`, 120-160 characters.             |

If `indexable: false`, also add a matching prefix to `ROBOTS_DISALLOW`.

## Copy lives in one place

A static page's hero copy belongs in `ui/src/lib/seo/content/staticPageCopy.ts`, imported by
the page **and** by the snapshot renderer. Never let the crawler HTML say something the page
does not, and never duplicate the string in the snapshot.

## Canonical origin

Canonical, `og:url`, robots `Sitemap:` and JSON-LD use `https://kamespace.com` through
`siteOrigin.ts`. Never `window.location.origin`, never the request host, never a preview URL.

## Before claiming done

```bash
bun run seo:generate-robots    # after touching ROBOTS_DISALLOW
bun run check:seo-routes
bun run test                   # seoMeta, publicRoutes, siteOrigin, snapshot, middleware
bun run seo:audit -- --origin https://<preview-url> --fail-on-error
```

